  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/ComplexRenalCyst">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>complex renal cyst</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel>complex renal cyst</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>A renal cyst whose contents are not uniformly fluid.</skos:definition>
    <cde:localId>FC-000015</cde:localId>
    <cde:nodeType>FindingClass</cde:nodeType>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/RenalCyst"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N2007f57cc8fd4f458eb501677d3f176b"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nc1b64006184745fbb146c459e0c392df"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Ncd099eae567340268b7406c86a30b171"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nac11f62277a642239b620a673b5ad2a6"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N5f536fea473646f195d428f49b4df2c8"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nfdb972f22cc447b0bc029b0fc81444fc"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N60b83b3f4802467fb62da44da34004fd"/>
    <cde:source>local</cde:source>
    <cde:sourceStatus>unrequested</cde:sourceStatus>
    <cde:designNote>Carries calcification; the parent does not. A simple cyst does not calcify, and a calcified renal cyst is Bosniak II or above, which is complex by definition.</cde:designNote>
    <cde:designNote>Defined class: conditions are necessary and sufficient, so a reasoner classifies into it. Nothing about it is authored twice.</cde:designNote>
    <cde:anchorVerdict>post_coordinated</cde:anchorVerdict>
